WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.380
WandaVision is intriguing for a number of
reasons, not the least of which is that one

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.620
of its main characters is currently dead.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.490
But we know better by now than to second-guess
Marvel, so despite the confusion, we're eager

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.659
to see what WandaVision has in store for us
when it hits Disney+.

00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:14.659
Release date

00:00:14.659 --> 00:00:19.500
During the company's Hall H presentation at
San Diego Comic Con in July of 2019, Marvel

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.390
Studios revealed a pretty packed calendar
for 2020 and '21, laying out plans for a whopping

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.590
ten new films and television series centered
around various characters in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.620
Universe.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.720
Originally, WandaVision was scheduled to be
the second of seven MCU projects premiering

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.070
in 2021, but those plans have been reworked
numerous times since then, with multiple unanticipated

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.470
delays altering the series’ release date.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:46.020
WandaVision initially moved its release up
to late 2020, before being pushed back to

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.160
2021 once again due to the ongoing delays
and disruptions caused by the coronavirus

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.160
pandemic.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.010
While WandaVision was originally intended
to be preceded in Phase 4 by the movie Black

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:59.260
Widow, the Disney+ series The Falcon and the
Winter Soldier, and another movie debuting

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:04.190
the Eternals team of superheroes, the space-and-time-twisting
series will now be the first entry in the

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.820
MCU's new chapter, with a premiere date set
for January 15, 2021.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.960
The shakeup comes as a result of the theatrical
releases for both Black Widow and Eternals

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.490
being delayed to later in 2021.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.390
On the TV side, the pandemic-related disruptions
caused The Falcon and the Winter Soldier to

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.729
experience production delays that made its
planned 2020 release impossible.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:27.350
Currently, WandaVision is the only one of
Marvel's upcoming Disney+ shows to have an

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.700
official release date.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.140
Originally, it was scheduled to lead right
into Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:37.940
the follow-up to 2016's Doctor Strange in
which Wanda Maximoff is said to play a significant

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.940
role.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.820
However, at least as far as the current schedule
is concerned, the two MCU properties may have

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.159
their releases separated by more than a year,
with Doctor Strange now being the last of

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:48.880
the Phase 4 films slated to hit theaters.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.470
"Time is the true enemy of us all.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.820
Time kills everything."

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:53.820
Main attraction

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.490
Alongside Disney's original announcement that
they would be making shows centered around

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:01.090
popular film characters came the confirmation
that Elizabeth Olsen would indeed be reprising

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.439
her MCU role on the small screen.

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:07.690
Olsen has been playing Scarlet Witch, a.k.a.
Wanda Maximoff, since Captain America: The

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:12.880
Winter Soldier, when she and her brother Quicksilver,
a.k.a. Pietro Maximoff were teased in a scene

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.510
at the end of the credits.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:18.340
Quicksilver was tragically killed at the end
of Avengers: Age of Ultron, but Wanda went

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.560
on to join the Avengers.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.709
While it's debatable which Avenger is the
most powerful, Wanda is a strong contender

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:27.560
for the title, and proved to be one of the
team's most effective weapons against Thanos.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:32.140
Her abilities in the MCU include telekinesis,
telepathy, and energy manipulation.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.780
In the comics, Wanda is an immensely powerful
magic user who can manipulate Chaos Magic,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.370
allowing her to alter reality.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.610
While we have yet to see that ability manifest
in the MCU, don't be surprised if WandaVision

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:45.610
delves deeper into the more mystical side
of her abilities.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:49.750
Co-starring alongside Olsen in WandaVision
will be her frequent MCU scene partner, Paul

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.709
Bettany, reprising his role as the android
Vision.

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:56.520
Of course, Bettany's inclusion is a little
surprising, since as of the end of Avengers:

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.879
Infinity War, Vision is dead — double-dead,
so maybe those reality-altering powers of

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:05.739
Wanda's have a little something to do with
this yet-unexplained development.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:09.610
Beyond his role on-screen as the Vision, Paul
Bettany has actually been with the MCU as

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.700
a voice actor from the very beginning.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.260
"JARVIS, you up?"

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.230
"For you, sir, always."

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.811
However, Vision wasn't introduced as a character
until 2015's Avengers: Age of Ultron, when

00:03:19.811 --> 00:03:23.780
Tony Stark's A.I. butler J.A.R.V.I.S. was
uploaded into an android body and brought

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.860
to life using the Mind Stone.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.760
Since then, Vision has fought alongside the
Avengers, with formidable powers including

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.129
superstrength, flight, energy blasts, and
density manipulation.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:37.120
Prior to Avengers: Infinity War, he also fell
in love with Wanda Maximoff, and the two were

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.940
hoping to start a life together before Thanos'
arrival put a tragic end to their plans.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.470
Vision was murdered by Thanos when the Mad
Titan ripped the stone from his head in order

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.070
to complete the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:50.930
However, it would appear that one way or another,
Vision will be resurrected in WandaVision.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.930
Supporting cast

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:56.220
Captain Marvel first introduced us to Monica
Rambeau, the school-aged daughter of Carol

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.560
Danvers' best friend, Maria.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.950
In the comics, Monica is a grown woman and
a superhero herself.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.520
She's gone by several codenames, including
Spectrum and her own version of Captain Marvel,

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.870
with Monica technically taking on the name
before Carol Danvers ever did.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:13.040
While we still don't know whether Monica will
be suiting up as Spectrum or one of her other

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.870
comic aliases, we now have confirmation that
an aged-up Monica will be entering the MCU

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.129
as part of the WandaVision cast.

00:04:19.129 --> 00:04:21.530
The adult Monica will be played by Teyonah
Parris.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.110
While no details have been revealed about
exactly how Monica will factor into WandaVision,

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:30.210
it seems likely that the events of the series
could lead to her receiving her powers, based

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.020
on what seems to be a hint by Parris at San
Diego Comic Con.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:37.789
"This is a dream, to be a Marvel superhero.”

00:04:37.789 --> 00:04:42.580
Also joining the cast of WandaVision are MCU
scene-stealers Kat Dennings and Randall Park.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.889
Dennings appeared in the first two Thor films
as Darcy Lewis, assistant to astrophysicists

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:48.819
Jane Foster and Eric Selvig.

00:04:48.819 --> 00:04:52.770
Darcy was last seen at the end of Thor: The
Dark World and wasn't even mentioned in Thor:

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.219
Ragnarok, making her return in WandaVision
a pleasant surprise.

00:04:56.219 --> 00:05:00.210
Helping round out the cast of WandaVision
will be Ant-Man and the Wasp's former S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.610
agent Jimmy Woo, played by Randall Park.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.010
Like Dennings, Park's role in his previous
MCU film was largely comedic, as the FBI agent

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:10.819
tasked with making sure Scott Lang stuck to
the restrictions of his house arrest.

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:14.530
It's hard to anticipate a scenario that would
lead Wanda and Vision to cross paths with

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:18.870
Woo and Darcy, but if there's one thing that's
becoming abundantly clear about WandaVision,

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.800
it's that it will be embracing the unexpected.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:21.800
Hark!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.800
Who goes there?

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.099
Rounding out the WandaVision cast is comedic
actress Kathryn Hahn, playing a character

00:05:25.099 --> 00:05:27.729
who has only been officially identified as
a "nosy neighbor."

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:32.279
However, while the subtitles on the WandaVision
trailer refer to her as Agnes, many clues

00:05:32.279 --> 00:05:35.419
point toward Hahn playing the sorceress Agatha
Harkness.

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:39.219
In the comics, Agatha and the Scarlet Witch
have a long and complicated history, with

00:05:39.219 --> 00:05:43.139
Agatha acting as Wanda's mentor and teaching
her how to use her magical powers.

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:46.789
But it's her interaction with Vision in the
WandaVision trailer that may offer the biggest

00:05:46.789 --> 00:05:48.490
clue to her role in the series.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.020
"Am I dead?"

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:53.080
"No, why would you think that?"

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.610
"Because you are."

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:59.240
In Tom King's The Vision comics, Agatha Harkness
is in fact dead, and it is her ghost who acts

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:03.259
as the narrator for the series, which serves
as a cautionary tale for Wanda.

00:06:03.259 --> 00:06:07.360
Since the WandaVision trailer shows Hahn jumping
through time alongside Wanda and Vision, she

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.789
may be serving a similarly omniscient role
here, which teases some dark possibilities

00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:13.039
for the seemingly upbeat series.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.039
A vision for WandaVision

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:18.800
The first and possibly the weirdest of Marvel's
slate of Disney+ shows will be helmed by television

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.029
director Matt Shakman, best known for his
work on the irreverent FX comedy series It's

00:06:23.029 --> 00:06:28.809
Always Sunny in Philadelphia, of which he
directed 43 episodes between 2007 and 2017.

00:06:28.809 --> 00:06:32.960
However, just because Shakman has some serious
comedy chops doesn't mean that WandaVision

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:35.719
will lack the epic stakes of the rest of the
MCU.

00:06:35.719 --> 00:06:39.999
Over his extensive career, Shakman has directed
his fair share of serious dramas, including

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:44.490
episodes of The Good Wife and Fargo, and has
even dabbled in superheroes, directing episodes

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:47.879
of Heroes Reborn and the recent Amazon original
series The Boys.

00:06:47.879 --> 00:06:52.589
He was also responsible for the Game of Thrones
season seven episode "The Spoils of War,"

00:06:52.589 --> 00:06:55.969
which featured the visually stunning "loot
train attack" sequence.

00:06:55.969 --> 00:07:00.539
Most recently, in 2020, Shakman was nominated
for an Emmy for his work on the pilot episode

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:02.749
of the Hulu period drama, The Great.

00:07:02.749 --> 00:07:06.729
Loosely based on the life of Catherine the
Great, the series deftly balanced history,

00:07:06.729 --> 00:07:09.659
comedy, high-stakes conflict, and emotional
drama.

00:07:09.659 --> 00:07:13.419
Given that WandaVision seems as though it
will be trying to pull off a similarly challenging

00:07:13.419 --> 00:07:17.469
juggling act, Shakman seems like the ideal
director to balance the power and emotional

00:07:17.469 --> 00:07:21.160
backstory of WandaVision's characters with
the show's weird and wacky tone.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.160
Time hopping

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:25.990
Although Vision was one of just a few fallen
heroes to not be resurrected at the end of

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:29.589
Avengers: Endgame, Marvel has confirmed that
WandaVision will be set after the Avengers'

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:32.490
final battle against Thanos in 2023.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:37.120
But the actual timeline for WandaVision may
be a lot more complicated than even that suggests,

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.169
with the trailer jumping through numerous
points in time from the 1950s to today.

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:46.500
In 2019, Elizabeth Olsen revealed that her
new series would be set in the 1950s, although

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:49.729
the trailer seems to indicate that's only
partially true.

00:07:49.729 --> 00:07:54.029
Yet for at least its first episode, the series
committed to its 1950s aesthetic, filming

00:07:54.029 --> 00:07:58.309
in front of a live studio audience, with the
crew members dressed in 1950s-era clothing.

00:07:58.309 --> 00:08:03.139
MCU mastermind Kevin Feige and WandaVision
director Matt Shakman even met with Dick Van

00:08:03.139 --> 00:08:07.469
Dyke while preparing for the show, asking
for any advice the iconic sitcom star could

00:08:07.469 --> 00:08:08.469
bestow.

00:08:08.469 --> 00:08:10.719
His response, based on his own experience,
was:

00:08:10.719 --> 00:08:13.909
"If it couldn't happen in real life, it couldn't
happen on the show."

00:08:13.909 --> 00:08:18.810
But that advice leaves room for some intriguing
applications on a reality-bending Marvel show.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:23.249
Those words of wisdom will surely be reinterpreted
for a series that seems to skip across decades

00:08:23.249 --> 00:08:25.179
as easily as a walk from room to room.

00:08:25.179 --> 00:08:26.179
No direct adaptations

00:08:26.179 --> 00:08:30.499
While fans have speculated that WandaVision
may draw from certain popular comic book storylines,

00:08:30.499 --> 00:08:34.120
Elizabeth Olsen said that WandaVision will
actually be pulling from a number of different

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.120
comics.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.519
So while many aspects of WandaVision may seem
familiar to comic fans, viewers probably shouldn't

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:43.830
expect the series to feel particularly beholden
to any individual storyline.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.629
Vision and Scarlet Witch have a long comics
history for Marvel Studios to pull from for

00:08:47.629 --> 00:08:51.240
their Disney+ series, leaving the door open
for a host of possibilities.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:55.100
Over the course of their existence in the
comics, the characters have been both heroes

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:59.180
and villains, and have gotten married, had
children, and faced all manner of opposition

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.670
from both enemies and allies.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:04.940
While a six-hour series probably doesn't leave
enough time for all of that, at least the

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:08.610
writers of WandaVision have no shortage of
material from which to draw inspiration.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.970
Leading to Doctor Strange

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:14.160
Originally scheduled to release in the spring
of 2021, WandaVision's six-episode run was

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.139
intended to end just as Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness swept into theaters

00:09:18.139 --> 00:09:19.139
that May.

00:09:19.139 --> 00:09:23.149
However, both have since been jostled around
on Marvel's calendar, and WandaVision will

00:09:23.149 --> 00:09:28.240
now be bowing on Disney+ in January of 2021,
while the Doctor Strange sequel won't hit

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.720
theaters until March 25, 2022.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:35.459
Still, despite the scheduling shake-up, the
two tales are likely to be closely linked.

00:09:35.459 --> 00:09:39.980
Elizabeth Olsen has been confirmed as a co-lead
of the Doctor Strange sequel, and Kevin Feige

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:44.190
teased that the events of WandaVision will
lead Wanda right to Stephen Strange's doorstep.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:47.420
"Allow me to help you."

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:51.019
There are a number of reasons why Wanda may
ultimately need assistance from the Master

00:09:51.019 --> 00:09:52.459
of the Mystic Arts.

00:09:52.459 --> 00:09:56.810
Given the title of the second Doctor Strange
film, it seems likely that the events of WandaVision

00:09:56.810 --> 00:10:00.649
will somehow contribute to the Multiverse
of Madness that Doctor Strange will be dealing

00:10:00.649 --> 00:10:02.460
with in his second solo outing.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:06.649
Whether Scarlet Witch and Doctor Strange wind
up as allies or opponents remains to be seen,

00:10:06.649 --> 00:10:10.579
but it's safe to assume that Wanda and Vision's
adventures in WandaVision are going to have

00:10:10.579 --> 00:10:13.210
some unforeseen — and possibly magical — consequences.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.570
Origin of "Scarlet Witch"

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:18.560
Even after playing a pivotal role in four
films, Wanda Maximoff has yet to be called

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:20.770
"Scarlet Witch" out loud in the MCU.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:24.870
The closest anyone has come to uttering her
codename was in Avengers: Age of Ultron, when

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.699
Tony Stark was trying to calm down Hulk.

00:10:26.699 --> 00:10:29.459
"That little witch is messing with your mind."

00:10:29.459 --> 00:10:33.459
Although she goes by both names interchangeably
in the comics, Wanda has always been referred

00:10:33.459 --> 00:10:35.110
to by her given name on screen.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:40.350
However, if Elizabeth Olsen's comments at
San Diego Comic Con in 2019 are any indication,

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:44.360
she will finally receive her official code
name in WandaVision, along with an explanation

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:47.149
for exactly why she goes by that moniker.

00:10:47.149 --> 00:10:51.209
Chances are, it has something to do with her
immense, potentially reality-shifting, magic-like

00:10:51.209 --> 00:10:54.860
powers, and the color of the energy she manipulates
with her hands.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:58.339
But even though the origin of her code name
seems rather obvious, it will still be nice

00:10:58.339 --> 00:11:01.259
to get explicit confirmation of her name and
its meaning within the MCU.

00:11:01.259 --> 00:11:03.329
"I don't even know who you are."

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:06.339
"You will."

00:11:06.339 --> 00:11:09.360
Sitcom inspiration

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.569
Frequently touted as the MCU's first sitcom,
the first trailers for WandaVision have revealed

00:11:13.569 --> 00:11:18.079
that not only will the Disney+ series be heading
into uncharted Marvel territory, but it will

00:11:18.079 --> 00:11:21.649
be paying homage to a number of familiar titles
in the process.

00:11:21.649 --> 00:11:25.089
Scattered amongst the brief glimpses of the
show we've seen so far have been what appears

00:11:25.089 --> 00:11:29.970
to be nods to a number of sitcom classics,
including Bewitched, The Brady Bunch, Roseanne,

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:33.550
Family Ties, I Love Lucy, and of course, The
Dick Van Dyke Show.

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:38.149
What it all means is more mysterious than
ever, but one thing is for certain: Paul Bettany

00:11:38.149 --> 00:11:41.470
was definitely not overstating anything when
he described the show as:

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.470
"F---ing bonkers."

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.470
Young Avengers?

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:47.389
The brief teaser for WandaVision shown during
the 2020 Super Bowl featured a short shot

00:11:47.389 --> 00:11:51.910
of Wanda and Vision looking down at two cribs,
then jumping as two pacifiers pop up into

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:52.990
the frame.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:57.329
The full trailer seems to confirm that these
are indeed Wanda and Vision's twin sons, Billy

00:11:57.329 --> 00:12:01.589
and Tommy, whose introduction in WandaVision
could have major repercussions not just for

00:12:01.589 --> 00:12:05.459
Wanda and Vision themselves, but for the rest
of the MCU as a whole.

00:12:05.459 --> 00:12:10.110
Of course, comics fans know that Billy and
Tommy play a huge role in multiple comics

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:11.110
storylines.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:14.769
Their disappearance leads to the popular "Avengers
Disassembled" and "House of M" storylines,

00:12:14.769 --> 00:12:18.259
both of which are significant comics events
with lasting repercussions.

00:12:18.259 --> 00:12:23.009
If any of those storylines are brought into
the MCU, the effects could be huge.

00:12:23.009 --> 00:12:26.590
In the comics, Billy and Tommy also grow up
to become two of the founding members of the

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.100
Young Avengers team.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:32.470
While their inclusion in WandaVision may not
seem significant yet, introducing the twins

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.639
leaves the door open for some pretty major
developments in the future.

00:12:35.639 --> 00:12:36.639
Story speculation

00:12:36.639 --> 00:12:40.329
As soon as it was announced that WandaVision
would have a 1950s aesthetic, some fans began

00:12:40.329 --> 00:12:44.181
speculating that it may adapt parts of Tom
King's run of comics for The Vision, which

00:12:44.181 --> 00:12:47.350
ran for 12 issues beginning in 2015.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:51.769
The Vision followed an entirely synthetic
family Vision had created for himself, consisting

00:12:51.769 --> 00:12:54.750
of his wife, Virginia, and their children,
Vic and Viv.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:59.089
The comic's themes centered around family,
normality and what it means to be truly human.

00:12:59.089 --> 00:13:02.920
As a family of synthetics, the Visions are
constantly in search of a better understanding

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.939
of life, driven by their desire to be seen
as normal.

00:13:05.939 --> 00:13:09.449
Although the specifics would need to change
for WandaVision, it's easy to see how these

00:13:09.449 --> 00:13:13.750
themes of humanity and family would fit into
a series about the MCU versions of Wanda and

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:14.750
Vision.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:18.250
After all, the last time these two characters
were together and happy in the MCU, they were

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:22.259
trying to figure out a way to share in a normal
life together, given their extraordinary abilities

00:13:22.259 --> 00:13:23.829
and circumstances.

00:13:23.829 --> 00:13:28.260
In another comics storyline, after Wanda's
children die, she alters the reality of Earth,

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.519
creating a new world in which they are alive.

00:13:30.519 --> 00:13:35.050
This new reality led to the highly acclaimed
"House of M" comics event, an alternate reality

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:37.990
arc created out of Wanda's grief and magic.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:42.509
That arc led into the less well-received "Decimation"
storyline, in which Wanda strips all mutants

00:13:42.509 --> 00:13:43.730
of their powers.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:48.800
"House of M" has long been popular among comics
fans, and has even been mentioned by MCU writers

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.180
Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely as
a storyline they considered adapting for inclusion

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.160
in either Infinity War or Endgame.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:59.700
The MCU version of Wanda doesn't have children
yet, although the WandaVision trailer hints

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:03.950
that that may soon change, but her grief over
the loss of Vision could work as a setup for

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.050
a similar story.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:09.100
A "House of M"-like premise could explain
not only Vision's resurrection in WandaVision,

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:11.199
but also the incongruous time periods.

00:14:11.199 --> 00:14:16.209
If Wanda is altering reality, maybe she keeps
reimagining what that reality looks like.

00:14:16.209 --> 00:14:20.010
While the lack of mutants in the MCU means
significant liberties would need to be taken

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:24.309
with any sort of "House of M" adaptation,
all the other pieces are in place for a grief-fueled

00:14:24.309 --> 00:14:27.509
story in which Wanda alters the world to bring
back someone she loves.

00:14:27.509 --> 00:14:28.509
Big promises

00:14:28.509 --> 00:14:32.829
Elizabeth Olsen has been vocal about her excitement
for her Disney+ series, telling the audience

00:14:32.829 --> 00:14:34.509
at Marvel's Comic Con presentation,

00:14:34.509 --> 00:14:37.540
"We're gonna go deep, we're gonna have lots
of surprises, and we're going to finally understand

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:43.920
Wanda Maximoff as the Scarlet Witch."

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.720
Wanda has been described as "weird" in the
MCU before, back when Agent Maria Hill was

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:51.430
first bringing Captain America up to speed
on Wanda and her brother's superpowers.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:55.110
"He's got increased metabolism and improved
thermal homeostasis.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:15:00.390
Her thing is neuroelectric interfacing, telekinesis,
manipulation…

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.629
He's fast and she's weird."

00:15:01.629 --> 00:15:05.319
However, we expect that when Olsen said the
series would be "weird," she wasn't simply

00:15:05.319 --> 00:15:09.339
referring to her existing powers, but something
brand new and bizarre that we've never seen

00:15:09.339 --> 00:15:10.850
before in the MCU.

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:13.519
Kevin Feige backed up Olsen's promises, telling
the audience,

00:15:13.519 --> 00:15:15.290
"Wait until you see this show.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.100
It's unlike anything we've done before."

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.920
And as for the Vision himself, Paul Bettany
thinks audiences are in for a unique treat

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:21.920
with WandaVision.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:28.760
"It's so funny and it just ends up being this
huge epic.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.779
The writing's so extraordinary."

00:15:30.779 --> 00:15:35.320
So while we may still not know exactly what
to expect from the weird world of WandaVision,

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:39.240
after seeing the excitement of everyone involved,
we're sure it will blow our minds.

